    "message": "Credit limit is stored once per customer, so for each order status I added up the credit limit of each distinct customer who has at least one order with that status. Totals: ok = 111,230 and bad = 92,580. A customer with orders in both statuses is counted under each one, so the two totals overlap and shouldn't be added together. If you instead add the credit limit once for every order, customers get counted many times and the totals become 2,381,120 (ok) and 327,270 (bad). One 'ok' entry, either an order with no matching customer or a customer with no credit value, adds nothing to its total."
